# L §6.1 "A member is closed ... a binding inside a member ranges over that member's things, the prelude's kinds
# included. The joint model's own bindings over a shared kind range over every member's things"; E §3.1 step 1 "a
# member that is itself a joint model pins its own members". a is a joint model of b: a's own count over accounts
# holds ka and b's kb (2), b's holds kb (1), and the outer joint model's own count holds both (2); asked inside the
# joint model, a.n and a.b.n answer as a and b answer alone, and the joint model's own n_a reads a's def (2).
=== J/joint.tally
model family
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
  use a = "../A" sha256 "b3c10393f906bea6e10e5d1cbc00844b20c76786e2f44e675f985312465f38bf"

source s "umowa"

input day: date

def all_n: int = count(x in accounts on day)

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-01-01
  day = 2026-06-01

ask n: all_n
ask n_a: a.cnt
=== A/reality.tally
model ana
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
  use b = "../B" sha256 "b8c6618f1d83400a72031f4896cca25609d34e47e3717e5eb533632484851d9c"

source s "umowa"

input day: date

def cnt: int = count(x in accounts on day)

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-01-01
  accounts + [ka] PLN lives 2026-01-01..
  day = 2026-06-01

ask n: cnt
=== B/reality.tally
model ben
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "umowa"

input day: date

def cnt: int = count(x in accounts on day)

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-01-01
  accounts + [kb] PLN lives 2026-01-01..
  day = 2026-06-01

ask n: cnt
=== expect n n_a a.n a.b.n
n: 2
  cut 2026-10-20
n_a: 2
  cut 2026-10-20
a.n: 2
  cut 2026-10-20
a.b.n: 1
  cut 2026-10-20
